/Title (Q2. What is the difference between Matplotlib and other visualization libraries? ANS:- Matplotlib is a fundamental data visualization library in Python used to create static, animated, and interactive plots. It provides detailed control over every element of a graph, but requires more coding. Other libraries like Seaborn and Plotly are built on top of Matplotlib and simplify the process of visualization by providing better default styles and advanced features. Thus, Matplotlib is mainly used when detailed customization is needed, while other libraries are preferred for quick and visually appealing plots.)
