/Title (Q3. What is the purpose of the pyplot module in Matplotlib? ANS:- The pyplot module is a collection of functions in Matplotlib that provides a simple interface for creating and managing plots. It allows users to create figures, plot data, and customize graphs step by step. Pyplot is widely used because it follows a procedural approach similar to MATLAB, making it easy for beginners to understand. It also helps in controlling various components of a graph such as axes, titles, labels, legends, and grid. Thus, pyplot acts as the main tool for visualization in Matplotlib.)
